<Routines>
<Routine Name="ClearAllNestTracking" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[//Created By Bill Hamby on 12/2/2019. Used for clearing all nest tracking data on the entire machine. Typicall created as a manual function only. This does NOT clear the Op (Operation) Status or nest performance data.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to \Chassis.Setup_NestQty do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[	COP (ZeroPartAssyStat, Data.Nest[iStaNum].PartStatus,1);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[	COP (ZeroProcessData, Data.Nest[iStaNum].ProcessData,1);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[	COP (ZeroProductData, Data.Nest[iStaNum].ProductData,1);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[End_for;]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The robots in this project are using tracking stations/nest 0 for the bobbin robot and 21 for the unload robot.. Therefore, the nest num at the station is loaded with a constant so it cannot be overwritten with the wrong number.

Bobbin Robot Station 0 Nest 0
Unload Robot station 21 Nest 21 ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(0,Data.Station[0].NestNum)MOV(21,Data.Station[21].NestNum);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[For the Nest located At The Last Station On The Main Chassis :
-Calculate Nest & Station Performance
-Copy data for data logging!!!!
-Clear Nest's Part Assembly Status Bits]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(CalcAndClearDataBit)ONS(OneShot.1)MOV(Setup_LastStationNestNum,StationNestNumTEMP)[JSR(NestPerformanceCalc,0) ,JSR(StationPerformanceCalc,0) ,XIC(AlwaysOn) [COP(ZeroPartAssyStat,Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus,1) ,COP(ZeroProcessData,Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].ProcessData,33) ,COP(ZeroProductData,Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].ProductData,1) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(debug_DES)ONS(OneShot.25)[COP(Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus,\Logging.NewData.PartStatus,1) ,COP(Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].ProcessData,\Logging.NewData.ProcessData,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The ProductData (stations required to operate by the running recipe) is copied from the current running recipe to the tracking data for the nest at the last station.
This must be set before the nest gets to the first operation station so the station knows if it should operate (because its looking at tracking data, not recipe data)

NOTE: Additional functionality was added to allow the Samples program to set the required station based on the sample requirements. Therefore, while the sample sequence is running, the required station bits are set in the Samples program instead of this one.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(CalcAndClearDataBit)ONS(OneShot.2)COP(\Recipe.Data.Running.AssemblyOp,Data.Nest[Setup_LastStationNestNum].ProductData,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[HMI_OutMom(HMI_ClearTrackingBits,1,2000,0,0,ClearTrackingVisibility,0,\Security.Level,15,1) JSR(ClearAllNestTracking,0) ,[XIO(SafeOK) XIO(\Mode.AutoModeMemory) ,XIC(\Mode.Manual) ,XIC(\Safety.EStopNOK) ] OTE(ClearTrackingVisibility) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Calls To Subroutines

NOTE: If Reject History Is Used It MUST Be Scanned Before Tracking Data Is Deleted]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(PartOverallStatus,0)JSR(ResetStationPerformance,0)JSR(ResetNestPerformance,0)JSR(StationFaultCount,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="NestPerformanceCalc" Type="ST">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tally All Nest Performance Counts For The Current Nest]]>
</Description>
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[bAttempt := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[bFailure := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[bSuccess := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//Increment Nest Att/Succ/Fail counters]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[//Modified By Bill Hamby on 11/2/2018. Combined Attempt and Failure FOR loops into one loop. Added functionality for Nest Deviation calculation.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to \Chassis.Setup_NestQty do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[	//At the last station, loop through all the station attempt bits and set the attempt bit if any one of its station attempt bits are set.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[	IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus.Station[iStaNum].Attempt) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[		bAttempt := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[		EXIT;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[End_for;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[//The extra FOR loop is needed because of the EXIT schema]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to \Chassis.Setup_NestQty do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[	//loop through all the station failure bits and set the nest failure bit if any one of its station failure bits are set.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[	IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus.Station[iStaNum].Failure) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[		bFailure := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[		EXIT;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[	//If a success is seen at any station]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[	IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus.Station[iStaNum].Success) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[		bSuccess := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[End_for;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[IF (bAttempt) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Attempts := Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Attempts + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[IF (bFailure) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Failures := Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Failures + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[	IF (bSuccess) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="36">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Successes := Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Successes + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="37">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="38">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="39">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="40">
<![CDATA[// Calculate Nest Efficiency after Att/Succ/Fail bits have been set for the Nest at the last station]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="41">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="42">
<![CDATA[IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Attempts > 0) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="43">
<![CDATA[	rEfficiencyTemp := (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Successes * 10000) / Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Attempts;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="44">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Efficiency := rEfficiencyTemp / 100;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="45">
<![CDATA[ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="46">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Efficiency := 100;	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="47">
<![CDATA[END_IF;	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="48">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="49">
<![CDATA[// Calculate Nest Deviation. This is a measure of how much an individual nest's efficiency deviates from the average efficiency of all the nests.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="50">
<![CDATA[//    This shows outlier nests.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="51">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="52">
<![CDATA[rNestAveEfficiencyTemp := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="53">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to \Chassis.Setup_NestQty do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="54">
<![CDATA[	//Add up all the efficiencies of the nests ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="55">
<![CDATA[	rNestAveEfficiencyTemp := rNestAveEfficiencyTemp + Data.Nest[iStaNum].PerformData.Efficiency;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="56">
<![CDATA[End_for;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="57">
<![CDATA[	//divide by the number of total nests to find the total average efficiency]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="58">
<![CDATA[	NestAveEfficiency := rNestAveEfficiencyTemp / \Chassis.Setup_NestQty;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="59">
<![CDATA[// Find the deviation from the average]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="60">
<![CDATA[IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Efficiency <= NestAveEfficiency) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="61">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Deviation := NestAveEfficiency - Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Efficiency;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="62">
<![CDATA[Else]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="63">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Deviation :=  Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Efficiency - NestAveEfficiency;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="64">
<![CDATA[END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="65">
<![CDATA[// Change the fill color of the Deviation value displayed on the HMI]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="66">
<![CDATA[IF(Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Deviation > Preset_NestPerformHigh) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="67">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.HMIColorStatus := 3;  //high deviation]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="68">
<![CDATA[Elsif (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Deviation < Preset_NestPerformHigh) AND (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.Deviation >= Preset_NestPerformLow)  THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="69">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.HMIColorStatus := 2;   //moderate deviation]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="70">
<![CDATA[Else]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="71">
<![CDATA[	Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PerformData.HMIColorStatus := 1;   //low deviation]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="72">
<![CDATA[End_if;]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="PartOverallStatus" Type="ST">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Sets The Part Status Good or Bad
Staus Bit In Tracking Data]]>
</Description>
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[//NOTE: Logic copied from job 846 Subaru Chassis. Logic for job 859 Novi Tester utilized Process OpOrder functionality. That was not needed for this machine, so simpler logic was used. -W.E.H. 4/25/2021]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//Written By Dave Shaner and Bill Hamby 4/27/2017]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[//Modified By W.E.H. 1/18/2018 to have tracking in its own seperate program (removed from Chassis)]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[//Modified by Saggio and Hamby 5-23-2018 Added check for missed opportunity when required, also added else statement at end to load zeros into part status,]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[//                                       Added Overall check for part loaded before checking success/failure bits]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[//Modified by Bill Hamby 11/27/2018  Added check for when reject station is located before the good. Part remains good when the reject doesn't cycle.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[//Check part status data at all stations to set the good or bad overall part status bit]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[// ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[//Inverted logic was used to make the code structure simpler]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[For dStationNum := 0 to  \Chassis.Setup_NestQty By 1 Do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[	bNestSuccess := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[	bNestFailure := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[	bNestRecycled := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[	myNestNum := Data.Station[dStationNum].NestNum;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[	CheckPriorStaNum := dStationNum-1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[	//Check Stations Before and up to the current one]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[	For dStationNum2 := 0 to  dStationNum By 1 Do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[		If (Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.PartLoaded AND Data.Nest[myNestNum].ProductData.StationRequired[dStationNum2] AND (dStationNum2 <> Setup_RejectStaNum)) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[			If (Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Recycle AND NOT Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Bypass) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[				bNestFailure := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[				bNestSuccess := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[				bNestRecycled := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[				Exit; //Exits the inside (station) for loop]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="36">
<![CDATA[			ELSIf (Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Failure AND NOT Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Bypass) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="37">
<![CDATA[				bNestFailure := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="38">
<![CDATA[				bNestSuccess := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="39">
<![CDATA[				Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Recycled := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="40">
<![CDATA[				Exit; //Exits the inside (station) for loop]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="41">
<![CDATA[//			ELSIf (Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Success AND NOT Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Bypass) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="42">
<![CDATA[			ELSIf (Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Success OR Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Bypass) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="43">
<![CDATA[				bNestFailure := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="44">
<![CDATA[				bNestSuccess := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="45">
<![CDATA[				bNestRecycled := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="46">
<![CDATA[			//Only Check following condition for previous stations. This is the case when the station didn't cycle, but it was supposed to.	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="47">
<![CDATA[			ELSIf (dStationNum2 < dStationNum) Then ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="48">
<![CDATA[				If (NOT Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Success AND NOT Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Failure AND NOT Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Station[dStationNum2].Bypass) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="49">
<![CDATA[					bNestFailure := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="50">
<![CDATA[					bNestSuccess := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="51">
<![CDATA[					bNestRecycled := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="52">
<![CDATA[					Exit; //Exits the inside (station) for loop]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="53">
<![CDATA[				End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="54">
<![CDATA[			]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="55">
<![CDATA[			End_if;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="56">
<![CDATA[		End_if;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="57">
<![CDATA[	End_for;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="58">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="59">
<![CDATA[	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="60">
<![CDATA[	If (bNestRecycled) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="61">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Bad := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="62">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Good := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="63">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Recycled := 1;	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="64">
<![CDATA[	ELSIf (bNestSuccess) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="65">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Bad := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="66">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Good := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="67">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Recycled := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="68">
<![CDATA[	ELSIf (bNestFailure) Then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="69">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Bad := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="70">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Good := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="71">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Recycled := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="72">
<![CDATA[	Else]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="73">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Bad := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="74">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Good := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="75">
<![CDATA[		Data.Nest[myNestNum].PartStatus.Recycled := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="76">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="77">
<![CDATA[	End_if;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="78">
<![CDATA[End_for;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="79">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="ResetNestPerformance" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[//Written By Bill Hamby 6/09/2018]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[//This routine handles resetting nest performance data when the reset button is pressed on the HMI. Each nest has an individual reset button and there is also a reset all button.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//The HMI_OutMom AOI was used in this logic so press hold and permissions could be assigned to the buttons.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[HMI_OutMom(HMI_ClearNestPerform,1,2000,0,AlwaysOff,AlwaysOn,0,\Security.Level,10,1); //HMI momentary button for clearing all nest perfrmance data]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to  \Chassis.Setup_NestQty By 1 Do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[	HMI_OutMom(Data.Nest[iStaNum].PerformData.HMI_Reset,1,2000,0,AlwaysOff,AlwaysOn,0,\Security.Level,10,1); //HMI momentary button for individual nest reset]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[	If (Data.Nest[iStaNum].PerformData.HMI_Reset.EnableOut OR HMI_ClearNestPerform.EnableOut)  then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[		COP(ZeroArrayPerformNestData,Data.Nest[iStaNum].PerformData,1);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[End_For;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="ResetStationPerformance" Type="ST">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clears individual or all station performance when buttons on  HMI are pushed]]>
</Description>
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[//Written By Bill Hamby 7/13/2018]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[//This routine handles resetting station performance data when the reset button is pressed on the HMI. Each station has an individual reset button and there is also a reset all button.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//The HMI_OutMom AOI was used in this logic so press hold and permissions could be assigned to the buttons.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[HMI_OutMom(HMI_ClearStationPerform,1,2000,0,AlwaysOff,AlwaysOn,0,\Security.Level,0,1); //HMI momentary button for clearing all station perfrmance data]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to  \Chassis.Setup_NestQty By 1 Do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[	HMI_OutMom(Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.HMI_Reset,1,2000,0,AlwaysOff,AlwaysOn,0,\Security.Level,10,1); //HMI momentary button for individual station reset]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[	If (Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.HMI_Reset.EnableOut OR HMI_ClearStationPerform.EnableOut)  then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[		COP(ZeroArrayPerformNestData,Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData,1);]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[End_For;]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="StationFaultCount" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[//Written By Bill Hamby 6/09/2018]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[//]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to  \Chassis.Setup_NestQty By 1 Do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[	IF \Mode.AutoPulse then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[		OneShotBit[iStaNum] := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[	IF \Mode.Auto then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[		IF Data.Station[iStaNum].OpStatus.Faulted AND NOT OneShotBit[iStaNum] then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[			OneShotBit[iStaNum] := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[			Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.FaultCount := Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.FaultCount + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[		ElSIf NOT Data.Station[iStaNum].OpStatus.Faulted then]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[			OneShotBit[iStaNum] := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[		End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[	End_If;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[End_For;]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="StationPerformanceCalc" Type="ST">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tally Station Performance Counts for the Current Nest]]>
</Description>
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[For iStaNum := 1 to \Chassis.Setup_NestQty do]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[	//At the last station, loop through all the station attempt, success, and failure bits and increment the station counters if the bits are set.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[	IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus.Station[iStaNum].Attempt) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Attempts := Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Attempts + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[	IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus.Station[iStaNum].Success) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Successes := Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Successes + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[	IF (Data.Nest[StationNestNumTEMP].PartStatus.Station[iStaNum].Failure) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Failures := Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Failures + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[/*	IF (Data.Head[LastStationNestNum].PartStatus[dStationNum].Recycle) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[dStationNum].PerformData.Attempts := Data.Station[dStationNum].PerformData.Attempts + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[dStationNum].PerformData.Failures := Data.Station[dStationNum].PerformData.Failures + 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[*/]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[//Calculate Station Efficiency after Att/Succ/Fail bits have been set for the Nest at the last station]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[	IF (Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Attempts > 0) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[		rEfficiencyTemp := (Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Successes * 10000) / Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Attempts;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Efficiency := rEfficiencyTemp / 100;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[	ELSE]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Efficiency := 0;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[	END_IF;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[	IF(Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Efficiency < Preset_StaPerformLow) THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.HMIColorStatus := 3;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[	Elsif (Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Efficiency < Preset_StaPerformHigh) AND (Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.Efficiency >= Preset_StaPerformLow)  THEN]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.HMIColorStatus := 2;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[	Else]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[		Data.Station[iStaNum].PerformData.HMIColorStatus := 1;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[	End_if;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[End_for;]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
